    referenceEn: "Moving to Saigon for a new job at twenty-four, I was stunned to discover how quickly rent, meals, and commuting could cost an arm and a leg. During my first six months, half my paycheck vanished within two weeks on trendy cafes and late-night food deliveries. Realizing I had zero savings, I decided to tighten my belt for a three-month reset. Whenever boredom struck on weekends, I stuck to window shopping without carrying a credit card. Instead of chasing flimsy bargains, I chose decent everyday essentials that stayed reliable without constant replacement. Surprisingly, after a year of mindful habits, watching my monthly profit margin—the savings left after expenses—grow felt far more rewarding than impulsive parcels at my door. My budget became genuinely stable, giving me the freedom to invest in an impressive professional course and build an emergency cushion for the road ahead.",
