    referenceEn: "Working freelance from Dalat for a European studio means my schedule sits six hours apart from my teammates. On stormy highland evenings, an unstable network can feel extremely frustrating when uploading heavy design files overnight. To avoid losing days of work, I strictly back up every project folder to an external drive before shutting down. Ahead of major English video reviews, I like to read aloud my presentation notes two or three times alone in my room. Having to talk to yourself in front of a quiet monitor may look funny at first, yet that rehearsal makes my pacing steady when the real call begins. Thankfully, my upgraded microphone worked perfectly throughout this week's review. Tools make it effortless to keep in touch across continents, but thoughtful preparation and punctual calls are what actually build lasting trust.",
