    "referenceEn": "Every Saturday afternoon, Mr. Hai paints his face white and performs mime near the park fountain during families' weekend outings. Without uttering a single word, he tells humorous stories purely through expressive eyes and fluid hand gestures. At first, passersby seem lethargic and apathetic, yet within minutes, children's laughter draws everyone to stop and watch. What saddens him most is not the uncertain income, but people's habit of littering after each show. Therefore, before wrapping up his act, he always mimes picking up empty bottles and tossing them into a bin to remind spectators to protect the public space.",
