    "referenceEn": "Shifting to a hybrid model split between office desks and home workspaces helps companies trim real estate overhead while cutting commute times. Yet the hardest hurdle lies in onboarding recent graduates entering the workforce for the first time. Relying solely on instant messages and video calls often leaves newcomers feeling isolated and hesitant to ask quick questions about internal workflows. To bridge this invisible gap, many forward-thinking firms now assign an experienced advisor to mentor each new hire during their first ninety days. Every week, the pair meets in person to review progress, clarify official regulations, and talk through unexpected challenges. Blending technological flexibility with deliberate human connection helps new employees settle into their duties smoothly while fostering lasting commitment.",
