    "referenceEn": "Scrolling through young people's feeds today, one easily encounters endless photos flaunting luxury watches, business-class flights, and lavish parties. Algorithm-boosted show-off culture leaves many viewers secretly envious and insecure about their own ordinary routines. What begins as sharing small milestones gradually morphs into an exhausting race to prove status. Psychologists warn that glorifying superficial wealth can breed anti-social resentment among peers who feel left behind. Failing to achieve instant material success like online idols, some grow frustrated, disillusioned, or contemptuous of honest everyday work. Ultimately, lasting peace belongs to those who feel genuinely content with steady personal growth and measure worth through meaningful community contributions.",
